### Algorithms and flowcharts

# Algorithms = A step-by-step procedure for solving a problem or accomplishing a task. It is a finite set of well-defined instructions that can be followed to achieve a specific goal.
# Flowcharts = A visual representation of an algorithm or processs, using arrows or "FLOW LINES" to show the flow. (BASICALLY A STRAIGHT ARROW)
# Two types of flowcharts:
# 1. Program flowchart = acts like mirrors in computer programs, contains the steps of solving a problem and logic and flow of code per module
"""Program flowcharts are an extremely useful tool in program development
First, any error can be easily detected and corrected in the flowchart before the program is written.
Second, a flow chart is easy to follow and explain.
And Third, this serves as a documentation of the program""" 

# RULES TO FOLLOW IN PROGRAM FLOWCHARTS
# Only standard symbols must be used in flowcharts
# The order of the flowchart should be top to bottom and LEFT to right
# Each symbol used in a flowchart should only have one entry point and one exit point only.
# The operations should be expressed independently of any particular programming language (Pseudocode)
# All decisions should be well labelled
 
# Flowchart Standard Symbols:
"""1. Terminal - Resembles the start and the end of the flowchart, should only be TWO.
2. Input/Output - shows any input or output operations. (PARALLELOGRAM SHAPE) (input num1, num2)
3. Processing Symbol - denotes to show any computer processing (RECTANGLE SHAPE) (ex. sum = num1 + num2)
4. Predefined Process - shows any process not specially defined in the flowchart 
5. Comment - used to write any statement used to clarify something
6. Flow line - used to connect the symbols
7. Document Input/Output - same as "Input/Output" but everything that you do is either coming from a document or you are putting it in a document
8. Decision - used to show any point in a process where a decision must be made (Usually used for conditional statements)
9. On-page connector - used to connect parts in the flowchart continued on the same page (KIND OF LIKE A PORTAL) (denoted by a circle).
10. Off-page connector -  used to connect parts in the flowchart continued on another page (denoted by a diamond shape thing)."""

# 2. System flowchart = collection of program flowcharts, contains solution of many problems together that are closely related to each other and interact with each other to achieve a goal
